er/id #uuid "e1498b41-ea7b-5297-b0d9-57e9714e3802" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415354} :answer-field/id #uuid "09b0eb5f-c65b-5b03-8dcb-9c5edf19b005" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415362}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c9d728b0-5a87-57b1-8b30-46d4db7caf62" :question/math-academy-id "q-213354" :question/problem "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $23,$ the additive inverse of $-49$ modulo $23$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of $-49$ modulo $23$ is the integer $0\\le x<23$ such that\n\n$$\nx+(-49)≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,23).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note that $-49≡20\\,(\\text{mod}\\,23):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-49 & ≡(-3)\\cdot 23+20 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23) \\\\  & ≡(-3)\\cdot 0+20 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23) \\\\  & ≡20 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, note that $-20+20≡0,$ so $x≡-20\\,(\\text{mod}\\,23).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-20 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23) \\\\  & ≡0-20 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23) \\\\  & ≡23-20 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23) \\\\  & ≡3 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,23)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $-49$ modulo $23$ is $3.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-49+3≡-46≡(-2)\\cdot 23≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,23)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** In general, the additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415396 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152065 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c91373a9-4a84-52ea-a77a-16beabf09acb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Additive Inverse of a Negative Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bc640fb-3a5b-558b-8451-0fb89a109109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bc640fb-3a5b-558b-8451-0fb89a109109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415330} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8dc1520-5543-5aaa-80d6-e9957a8c2135" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415379}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6564674d-f4f6-54d7-8b5f-5cfc473b8c8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-213355" :question/problem "Expressed as a nonnegative integer smaller than $8,$ the additive inverse of $-30$ modulo $8$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The additive inverse of $-30$ modulo $8$ is the integer $0\\le x<8$ such that\n\n$$\nx+(-30)≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).\n$$\n\nFirst, we note that $-30≡2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-30 & ≡(-4)\\cdot 8+2 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡(-4)\\cdot 0+2 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡2 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, note that $-2+2≡0,$ so $x≡-2\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8).$ To write this in the required form, we use the following sequence of congruences:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ≡-2 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡0-2 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡8-2 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8) \\\\  & ≡6 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of the element $-30$ modulo $8$ is $6.$\n\nWe can verify this result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-30+6≡-24≡(-3)\\cdot 8≡0\\,\\,✓\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** In general, the additive inverse of $a$ modulo $n$ is simply the residue of $-a$ modulo $n,$ i.e. $-a\\,\\text{mod}\\,n.$"}] [{